+        #
+        # These are registered rather than combinational. `tx_allowed` fans out to every endpoint
+        # interface and gates the decision to transmit, so a combinational `counter == N` puts the
+        # comparator and its whole fanout at the head of the transmit cone -- on a design that
+        # fills its device, that is the first two LUT levels of the longest path in it. Comparing
+        # against N - 1 a cycle earlier and flopping the result places each strobe on exactly the
+        # cycle it was on before, with the comparator behind a register.
         #
